# Build your first component

**Prerequisites:** [Install Rocci](/docs/start/install/) and
[Rocci in five minutes](/docs/start/five-minutes/).
**You will build:** a mental model of the styling example, not a second copy
of it.
**Starting files:** `examples/rocci/standalone/styling/Styling.rocci` in the
checkout.
**Time:** about twenty minutes.
**Verify:** `Hello` previews, the full page serves, and inspect output lists
components and fixtures.
**Next:** continue learning with the first standalone app, or look up
[language reference](/docs/reference/rocci/).

The canonical complete source is the cataloged styling app. This tutorial
does not paste a divergent copy under `docs/`. Open
[Styling](/examples/styling/) and
[Styling.rocci](/examples/styling/source/Styling-rocci/) beside this page.

## 1. Read the Hello component

`Hello` takes a props record. `name ?? "Roc"` is a defaulted field. A
self-closing `<Hello />` uses the default; `<Hello name="Foo"/>` overrides it.
The `@css` block is component-scoped: lowering stamps `data-rocci-css` and
wraps rules in CSS `@scope`.

That component is **pure**. It cannot log, open SQLite, or read the request.

## 2. Fixtures are preview data

```rocci
@fixture{target: Hello}
helloTest = { name: "Ada" }
```

Fixtures are ordinary Roc bindings tagged for `rocci view` and `rocci browse`.
They do not change the generated component function.

## 3. Inspect lowering

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- inspect --ast \
  examples/rocci/standalone/styling/Styling.rocci
```

**Verify:** the output names `Hello`, `FeatureCard`, and `StylePage`, lists
the fixtures, and prints source-map segments. `--ast` adds the parse tree.
There is no `--segments` flag; segments always print.

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- build \
  examples/rocci/standalone/styling/Styling.rocci
```

**Verify:** generated Roc contains `hello`, `featureCard`, and `stylePage`.

## 4. Preview the fixture

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- view \
  examples/rocci/standalone/styling/Styling.rocci \
  --component Hello
```

**Verify:** **Hello, Ada** from `helloTest`. Pass `--arg name=Roc` to override.

`rocci view` ignores HTTP declarations. `@view("/")` in this file is for
`rocci run`, not for `--component Hello`.

## 5. Run the document

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- run \
  examples/rocci/standalone/styling/Styling.rocci
```

**Verify:** a full page with file-level dark chrome, two Hello greetings, and
a feature card whose `output` shows `3`. File-level `@css` styles `body`, not
`html`. Headless:

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- run \
  examples/rocci/standalone/styling/Styling.rocci \
  --no-window
curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8000/ | grep -E 'data-rocci-css|hello-list|feature-card'
```

## Ability checklist

After this tutorial you can:

- Point `rocci view` at a PascalCase component and a fixture
- Explain that lowering produced Roc, not a custom runtime
- Distinguish file-level CSS from component-scoped CSS
- Find the complete source on the generated examples page

## What Rocci did

| You wrote | Rocci produced |
| --- | --- |
| `@component Hello` | `hello` returning `Html` |
| `@css` beside the markup | Scoped style metadata and a `<style>` inject for preview |
| `@fixture` | Indexed preview data |
| `@view("/")` | A GET document handler for `rocci run` |

